    no: 37,
    kind: 'correction',
    field: 'psalm.la',
    printed: 'Deus ad virtutem converte nos',
    used: 'Deus virtutum',
    why: 'The page adds "ad", which the psalter does not have, and reads the accusative "virtutem" where the psalter has the genitive: "Deus virtutum, converte nos" (Psalm 79:8), the God of hosts. Kircher\'s table, which Lenain cites for the verses, has "virtutum" in another verse of the same psalm: it gives the refrain in its last form, "Domine Deus virtutum, converte nos" (79:20, which it cites as 79:4; Oedipus Aegyptiacus II.1, p. 278), so it witnesses the word, not Lenain\'s verse 8. This field gives the verse as the psalter has it; the entry\'s French keeps what the page prints. The 1823 printing has “Deus virtutem converte nos” (p. 69). The added "ad" is the reissue\'s, from its resetting; "virtutem" is in both printings, so it is Lenain\'s or his printer\'s.',
